  "question": {
    "text": "Let $a_1, a_2, a_3, \\ldots$ be terms of an A.P. If $\\frac{a_1+a_2+\\cdots a_p}{a_1+a_2+\\cdots+a_q}=\\frac{p^2}{q^2}, p \\neq q$, then $\\frac{a_6}{a_{21}}$ equals",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "u72ne",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{41}{11}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3QlIY",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{7}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hXzuH",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{2}{7}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pFMBa",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{11}{41}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{\\frac{p}{2}\\left[2 a_1+(p-1) d\\right]}{\\frac{q}{2}\\left[2 a_1+(q-1) d\\right]}=\\frac{p^2}{q^2} \\Rightarrow \\frac{2 a_1+(p-1) d}{2 a_1+(q-1) d}=\\frac{p}{q} \\\\\n& \\frac{a_1+\\left(\\frac{p-1}{2}\\right) d}{a_1+\\left(\\frac{q-1}{2}\\right) d}=\\frac{p}{q}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nFor $\\frac{a_6}{a_{21}}, p=11, q=41 \\rightarrow \\frac{a_6}{a_{21}}=\\frac{11}{41}$",
    "image": null
  },
